# zeocore-examples -- example environment configuration.
#
# Neither app in this repo needs ANY of these to run its dummy-data demo
# (`python run_demo.py` in either apps/ subdirectory). This file documents
# what a REAL live-testing session -- extending either app to talk to a
# real external service instead of local CSV/DuckDB -- would need.
#
# Pattern chosen (provisional -- see zeocore-dogfooding-DESIGN-02-secrets-
# and-config-pattern.md, still an open design fork at the time this file was
# written): a plain .env + .env.example, independent of zeocore's own
# zeo_core.config module. Copy this file to `.env`, fill in real values
# LOCALLY ONLY, and never commit `.env` (already in .gitignore).
#
# ZERO real values below. Every value here is a placeholder.

# --- apps/data_cleaning -----------------------------------------------
# The dummy-data demo (run_demo.py) needs none of this -- it reads/writes
# local CSV files only. The ORIGINAL agency-data-onboarding-kit also has a
# Postgres/Supabase storage layer this rebuild does not (yet) implement; if
# a future round adds it, this is the shape it would need:
DATA_CLEANING_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
DATA_CLEANING_SUPABASE_KEY=your-supabase-service-role-key-here

# --- apps/metrics_tracker ----------------------------------------------
# The dummy-data demo (run_demo.py) needs none of this -- it creates a local
# DuckDB file in a temp directory. No real external service is used by this
# app today; this placeholder exists only in case a future round adds one
# (e.g. a hosted DuckDB/MotherDuck target instead of a local file):
METRICS_TRACKER_DB_PATH=./metrics_tracker.db

# --- apps/data_cleaning: real Google Drive integration (round 2, ---------
# RULING-280 / CHARTER-03) -------------------------------------------------
# The dummy-data demo (run_demo.py) needs none of this. The OPTIONAL
# real-integration demo (run_demo_drive.py) needs all three -- see
# SETUP.md at the repo root for the full Google Cloud OAuth walkthrough
# that produces these values. Passed as plain environment variables
# (run_demo_drive.py reads os.environ directly, not this .env file, since
# neither app wires python-dotenv today) -- shown here so the SHAPE of
# what's needed is documented in one place. Never a real path/value here.
ZEOCORE_DRIVE_CLIENT_SECRETS=/path/to/your/client_secret.json
ZEOCORE_DRIVE_CREDENTIALS=/path/to/your/token.json
ZEOCORE_DRIVE_FILE_ID=your-google-drive-file-id-here
